@xiangxinhello please make sure you have installed this particular version of transformers
`pip install git+https://github.com/huggingface/transformers.git@21fac7abba2a37fae86106f87fcf9974fd1e3830`.

This was documented at https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/models/supported_models.html#multimodal-language-models

> Occasionally I get much longer response time like 15 seconds (especially when I use the same prompt as yours which instructs the model to explain in more detail), but in those cases the output text is also much longer than usual.偶尔我会得到更长的响应时间，比如15秒（尤其是当我使用与你的相同提示，让模型详细解释时），但在这些情况下，输出文本也比平时更长。

here is my request code:
```
chat_response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="Qwen__Qwen2-VL-7B-Instruct",
    messages=[
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "image_url",
                    "image_url": {
                        "url": f"data:image/jpeg;base64,{image_base64}",
                    },
                },
                {"type": "text", "text": question},
            ],
        },
    ],
    extra_body={    
        "trace_id": 'xasdad123',
        "top_k":100,
        "best_of":3,
        "do_sample": False
    },
    max_tokens=100,
    temperature=0.8,
    top_p=0.8,
    frequency_penalty=1.5,
)
```

> @fyabc Hi, I've noticed that in the Qwen2 VL chat template, there is no '\n' after <|vision_end|>, but there is one when launched through the vllm API server. This seems to be a bug.

@chenzhengda Hi, by default all mm placeholders are joined with "\n" separator (see `vllm.entrypoints.chat_utils._parse_chat_message_content_parts` for detailed implementation). It seems that we need to refactor `chat_utils.py` to fix this bug.
@ywang96 @DarkLight1337 Please also take a look at this problem and check my comments.
